  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A number XXX is called bad if its binary representation contains odd number of 111 bits. For example, X=13=(1101)2X = 13 = (1101)_2X=13=(1101)2​ is bad while X=3=(11)2X = 3 = (11)_2X=3=(11)2​ is not bad.\n\nChef calls an array AAA of length NNN **special** if the following conditions hold:\n\n\nFor each 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N, 0≤Ai&lt;2200 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{20}0≤Ai​&lt;220\nAll the elements of AAA are **distinct**\nThere does not exist any non-empty subset of AAA such that the bitwise XOR of the subset is bad.\nFor example,\n\n\nA=[2,3,4]A = [2, 3, 4]A=[2,3,4] is not **special** because the XOR of the subset [2,3][2, 3][2,3] is 2⊕3=12 \\oplus 3 = 12⊕3=1, which is bad. (⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation)\nA=[3,3]A = [3, 3]A=[3,3] is not special because its elements are not distinct.\nA=[3,5]A = [3, 5]A=[3,5] is special because it satisfies all the conditions.\nChef challenges you to construct **any** special array of length NNN. Can you complete Chef's challenge?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the special array to be constructed.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single line containing NNN space-separated integers, denoting the elements of the special array of length NNN you constructed.\n\n\n**Note:** It can be proved that a special array of length NNN always exists under the given constraints.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2200 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{20}0≤Ai​&lt;220"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1\n2",
        "output": "6\n3 5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: There is only one non-empty subset of the given array, namely [6][6][6]. The XOR of this subset is 6=(110)26 = (110)_26=(110)2​, which is not bad.\nTest Case 222: The given array has three non-empty subsets, namely [3],[5][3], [5][3],[5], and [3,5][3, 5][3,5].\n\n[3][3][3] has XOR 3=(11)23 = (11)_23=(11)2​, which is not bad.\n[5][5][5] has XOR 5=(101)25 = (101)_25=(101)2​, which is not bad.\n[3,5][3, 5][3,5] has XOR 6=(110)26 = (110)_26=(110)2​, which is not bad.\n\nNone of the subsets have bad XOR, and the elements are distinct. Hence, the array is special."
      }
    ]
  },
